/* Generated by tools/build-docs-bundle.mjs. Edit assets/content/docs/ instead. */
(function () {
  'use strict';
  var bodies = {
  "overview/introduction": "\u003cp>CoreStructuresX 2026.1.1 is a Paper plugin for manual-start modular structures. Administrators assemble structure packs from WorldEdit or FastAsyncWorldEdit schematics, validate the pack, and choose the location and facing of the first module.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"what-it-does\">What it does\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Loads versioned YAML pack definitions and referenced \u003ccode>.schem\u003c/code> modules.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Reads \u003ccode>[CSX]\u003c/code> ORIGIN, CONNECTOR and COMMAND marker signs.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Selects weighted schematic candidates, then tries configured fallback and closing groups.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Expands automatically or from a saved player-proximity trigger.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Applies world-wide overlap checks, optional block whitelists, projected hard limits and bounded lookahead.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Persists modules, connectors, triggers, commands and paste progress as data-version-5 JSON.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"current-stack\">Current stack\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The build targets Java 21, Paper API 1.21.11 and WorldEdit Bukkit 7.4.3. At runtime, install WorldEdit or FastAsyncWorldEdit. Those coordinates describe the current build boundary; test the exact Paper and schematic-provider builds used by your server.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"start-here\">Start here\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Read \u003ca href=\"#/docs/instructions/before-you-configure\">Before you configure\u003c/a>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Follow \u003ca href=\"#/docs/instructions/quick-install-patterns\">Install and first test\u003c/a>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Validate the bundled \u003ccode>csx_test_pack\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Use the \u003ca href=\"#/docs/guides/pack-authoring\">pack authoring guide\u003c/a> for your own graph.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "overview/capabilities": "\u003ch2 id=\"capabilities\">Structure generation capabilities\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreStructuresX combines marked schematics, weighted module groups, two expansion modes, bounded chunked paste jobs and durable recovery state.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"marked-schematics\">Marked schematics\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A schematic may define one explicit ORIGIN, any number of one-use CONNECTOR markers, and optional COMMAND markers. CoreStructuresX transforms marker positions, block states, block-entity NBT and optional entities with the module rotation.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"automatic-generation\">Automatic generation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>AUTOMATIC\u003c/code> mode selects open connectors in the supported nearest-to-origin then FIFO order. The configured delay counts only stable scheduler samples. TPS or MSPT instability pauses progress and durably resets the remaining delay to the configured value.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"player-proximity\">Player proximity\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>PLAYER_PROXIMITY\u003c/code> mode saves a trigger for each eligible connector or command. A player must enter that trigger's positive radius in the same world. Each trigger activates only its own connector or command; marker signs do not need to remain in the pasted world.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"weighted-groups\">Weighted groups\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Each connector names a group. That group supplies weighted schematic entries. If normal candidates fail, fallback groups are tried in order. When a hard limit is reached, endpoint-only closing groups can resolve remaining connectors without deleting prior modules.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"command-markers\">Command markers\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A COMMAND marker chooses one weighted command entry and dispatches its commands as the server console. Immediate commands run after durable module finalization. Proximity commands wait for their saved trigger. Consumption is persisted before dispatch, providing at-most-once behavior.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"chunked-paste\">Chunked paste\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Paste jobs advance through block, block-entity NBT and optional entity phases under shared operation, time, job and chunk-load budgets. Jobs keep only a bounded window of plugin chunk tickets and release those tickets when paused, failed, stopped or shut down.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "overview/safety-model": "\u003ch2 id=\"preflight\">Candidate preflight\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Before queueing a module, CoreStructuresX transforms its bounds, checks the complete chunk footprint, verifies the radius from the structure origin, and evaluates collisions with generated modules, active jobs and persisted quarantines in the same world.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"projected-limits\">Projected hard limits\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>max-modules\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>max-open-connectors\u003c/code> include queued, running, paused and otherwise recoverable jobs. Candidate connectors are added and the consumed parent connector is removed in the projection before admission. \u003ccode>max-radius\u003c/code> applies to every transformed corner.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"block-checks\">Block whitelist and double pass\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>An enabled whitelist rejects a candidate when a target block is not replaceable. Optional double-pass overlap can reconsider an overlap with an already generated parent/module using real world blocks. It requires block checking and never bypasses a pending job reservation.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"lookahead\">Bounded lookahead\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Lookahead dry-runs future candidates to the configured depth with \u003ccode>ALL_CONNECTORS\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>ANY_CONNECTOR\u003c/code>. It is bounded by global node and time budgets. It does not mutate the world, reserve jobs, run real-block checks or replace closing behavior.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"closing\">Closing without destructive rollback\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>When enabled, a normal limit transition enters \u003ccode>CLOSING\u003c/code>. Closing entries must be endpoints with zero CONNECTOR markers. CoreStructuresX never removes generated modules automatically because prior blocks, fluids, NBT, entities, commands and later external edits cannot be restored losslessly.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"last-write-check\">Immediately-before-write check\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>When the pack enables block checking, the runtime performs another exact whitelist check immediately before each world write. A failure after mutation may quarantine the job footprint so later instances cannot overlap an uncertain region.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "overview/authoring-model": "\u003ch2 id=\"one-pack-one-structure\">One pack, one structure type\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A direct child directory of \u003ccode>plugins/CoreStructuresX/packs/\u003c/code> defines one pack. The pack id identifies its live instances and must be unique across every loaded folder.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"four-yaml-files\">Four YAML responsibilities\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"Pack file responsibilities\">\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>File\u003c/th>\u003cth>Responsibility\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>pack.yml\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Identity and confined paths to the other files and schematics directory.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>structure.yml\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Start group, facing, offsets, expansion mode, hard limits, checks and paste settings.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>groups.yml\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Weighted schematic entries, per-entry overrides, fallbacks and closing groups.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>commands.yml\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Optional weighted console-command groups used by COMMAND markers.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"schematics\">Schematics\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Referenced schematic paths must remain inside the configured schematics folder after lexical and real-filesystem resolution. Absolute paths, traversal and external links are rejected. Each schematic should use one ORIGIN marker or a deliberately saved clipboard origin.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"graph\">The module graph\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The start group chooses the first module. CONNECTOR markers name the group used by each next edge. Fallback groups provide alternative candidates; closing groups provide zero-connector endpoints. With the default resolvability check, every reachable connector group needs a finite path to an endpoint.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"small-first\">Start with the smallest complete graph\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Prove an entrance, a repeatable path and an endpoint before adding splits, stairs, commands, lookahead or parallel jobs. Validate and restart that small graph, then add one source of variation at a time.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "overview/runtime-state": "\u003ch2 id=\"instances\">Instances\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>An instance owns one structure origin, selected mode, generated modules, connectors, triggers, command records and paste journals. Its persisted id is also its canonical JSON filename.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"instance-states\">Instance states\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>CREATED\nEXPANDING\nAUTO_EXPANDING\nPAUSED\nSTOPPED\nCLOSING\nCOMPLETED\nBLOCKED\nFAILED\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>PAUSED\u003c/code> preserves active progress. \u003ccode>STOPPED\u003c/code> is terminal and accepted only without an active or recoverable job. \u003ccode>COMPLETED\u003c/code> requires every connector to be used or closed and no active job.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"connectors\">Connector states\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>OPEN\nPROCESSING\nUSED\nCLOSED\nBLOCKED\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Every PROCESSING connector must correspond to exactly one recoverable child job, and every recoverable child job must reference its PROCESSING parent connector.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"triggers\">Trigger states\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>ACTIVE\nDISABLED\nEXPIRED\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Triggers are persisted independently from marker signs, so proximity behavior survives marker replacement and restart.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"finalizing\">Durable finalization\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>FINALIZING\u003c/code> is a job phase, not a public instance state. The detached final state is committed before new modules, connectors, triggers, completion or immediate command dispatch become visible to the live runtime.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "overview/current-boundaries": "\u003ch2 id=\"supported-runtime\">Supported runtime boundary\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Java 21 or newer.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Paper 1.21.11 or newer as the maintained documented requirement.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>WorldEdit or FastAsyncWorldEdit installed and loaded.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>WorldEdit Bukkit 7.4.3 is the current compile target; FAWE has no pinned Maven version in this project.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003cp>These are source and documentation facts for version 2026.1.1. They are not a guarantee for every future Paper, WorldEdit or FAWE build.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"manual-start-only\">Manual start only\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreStructuresX does not hook biome generation, chunk generation, world-seed distribution or random terrain placement. Every instance begins through an administrator command.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"not-supported\">Not supported in v1\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Folia scheduling.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Destructive module backtracking.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Storage types other than local JSON.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Paste modes other than chunked jobs.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Automatic migration of an administrator's existing YAML to newly added defaults.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"work-in-progress\">Operational expectation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>CoreStructuresX is under active development. Test updates and packs in an isolated environment, back up worlds, pack files, configuration and instance JSON, and review release notes before replacing a JAR.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "instructions/before-you-configure": "\u003ch2 id=\"requirements\">Requirements\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Java 21+.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Paper 1.21.11+.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>CoreStructuresX 2026.1.1.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>WorldEdit or FastAsyncWorldEdit installed and loaded.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>A permission manager when operator-only defaults are not appropriate.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"backup-first\">Back up before world mutation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Before testing a new pack or plugin update, back up the affected worlds and the complete \u003ccode>plugins/CoreStructuresX/\u003c/code> directory. Keep configuration, pack YAML, schematics and \u003ccode>data/instances/\u003c/code> together in the recovery set.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"trusted-authors\">Trust boundary\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Only trusted administrators should author packs or receive start permission. Schematics modify world blocks and optional entities; COMMAND markers dispatch server-console commands after durable placement.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"validation-boundary\">Validation boundary\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Validation catches unsupported keys and modes, unsafe paths, missing references, marker defects, unresolved connector graphs and configured size limits. It cannot prove visual correctness, production performance, plugin interoperability or every runtime world condition.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"existing-yaml\">Existing YAML is not auto-merged\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>When a plugin update adds bundled keys, the existing server file is left unchanged. Compare it with the documented current default and add new settings deliberately.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "instructions/layout-overview": "\u003ch2 id=\"plugin-folder\">Plugin folder\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>plugins/CoreStructuresX/\n|-- config.yml\n|-- packs/\n|   |-- csx_test_pack/\n|   `-- &lt;pack-id&gt;/\n|       |-- pack.yml\n|       |-- structure.yml\n|       |-- groups.yml\n|       |-- commands.yml\n|       `-- schematics/\n|           `-- *.schem\n`-- data/\n    `-- instances/\n        `-- &lt;instance-id&gt;.json\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003ch2 id=\"definitions\">Pack definitions\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Files under \u003ccode>packs/\u003c/code> describe choices available to future generation. Keep every referenced YAML and schematic path inside its pack directory. Do not point a pack at external files through traversal, symbolic links, junctions or reparse points.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"live-state\">Live instance state\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Files under \u003ccode>data/instances/\u003c/code> are authoritative runtime state. They contain generated module records, connectors, triggers, command reservations, job phases, checksums and cursors. Never store instance JSON inside a pack folder.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"bundled-pack\">Bundled test pack\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The JAR contains \u003ccode>bundled-packs/csx_test_pack/\u003c/code> and an explicit file manifest. First start installs it atomically only when the administrator copy does not exist; later starts never overwrite that directory.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"editing\">Editing rules\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Do not replace schematics or pack definitions while an instance using them is actively pasting. Stop the server for manual JSON repair. Use reload only within the boundaries in the next article.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "instructions/quick-install-patterns": "\u003ch2 id=\"paper-server\">Paper server\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Stop Paper.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Install WorldEdit or FastAsyncWorldEdit.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Place \u003ccode>CoreStructuresX-2026.1.1.jar\u003c/code> in \u003ccode>plugins/\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Start Paper once.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Confirm \u003ccode>plugins/CoreStructuresX/config.yml\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>packs/csx_test_pack/\u003c/code> were created.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003ch2 id=\"first-validation\">First validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>/csx validate\n/csx packs list\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Fix every error before starting an instance. Warnings about an omitted ORIGIN mean the saved schematic clipboard origin will be used; confirm that position is intentional.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"controlled-start\">Controlled start\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Back up the test world and instance folder, choose an isolated area, then start the bundled pack:\u003c/p>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>/csx start csx_test_pack\n/csx instances list\n/csx instance info &lt;instance-id&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>A console sender must provide the world, integer coordinates and cardinal facing:\u003c/p>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>/csx start csx_test_pack world 100 64 100 SOUTH\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003ch2 id=\"restart-test\">Restart test\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>After a controlled placement, stop Paper normally and start it again. Confirm the instance loads, connectors and triggers remain present, and any trusted interrupted job resumes only when its recorded pack, schematic, recipe, transform and operation counts still match.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "instructions/reload-vs-restart": "\u003ch2 id=\"reloadable\">Reloadable changes\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Use \u003ccode>/csx reload\u003c/code> for global \u003ccode>config.yml\u003c/code> changes, new pack folders, corrected pack YAML, or schematic additions made before affected instances begin using them.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"reload-guard\">Reload guard\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Reload is rejected while any paste job is queued, running, paused or finalizing. A paused instance retains its exact cursor and still blocks reload. Wait for every paste job to finish.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>A rejected reload leaves the current runtime and scheduler in place. If loading a replacement configuration fails after schedulers stop, the plugin restores the previous config, packs, manager and schematic service, then restarts the previous scheduler.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"restart-required\">Restart required\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Replacing the CoreStructuresX JAR.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Replacing WorldEdit or FAWE.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Changing Paper or Minecraft version.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Recovering from startup dependency or classloading errors.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Performing a clean boot after broad configuration or pack changes.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"restart-recovery\">Restart recovery\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Normal shutdown persists every instance synchronously after flushing the ordered checkpoint writer. Startup reconstructs trusted jobs only when fingerprints, transforms and operation counts match. Changed recovery inputs block the job and parent connector instead of pasting unverified content.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "instructions/marker-signs": "\u003ch2 id=\"header\">Header\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Every marker begins with \u003ccode>[CSX]\u003c/code> on line 1. Header matching is case-insensitive by default. Supported line-2 types are exactly \u003ccode>ORIGIN\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CONNECTOR\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>COMMAND\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"origin\">ORIGIN\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>[CSX]\nORIGIN\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Use zero or one ORIGIN. Zero uses the saved schematic clipboard origin when \u003ccode>validation.require-origin\u003c/code> is false. More than one is invalid. The marker block is replaced during paste.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"connector\">CONNECTOR\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>[CSX]\nCONNECTOR\n&lt;group-id&gt;\n&lt;optional-radius&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Line 3 names a group from \u003ccode>groups.yml\u003c/code>. Optional line 4 is a positive player-proximity radius. A blank line uses the pack default; a nonblank zero, negative or malformed value is invalid. The sign facing determines the expansion direction.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"command\">COMMAND\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>[CSX]\nCOMMAND\n&lt;command-group-id&gt;\n&lt;optional-radius&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Line 3 names a group from \u003ccode>commands.yml\u003c/code>. In automatic mode the command is considered after durable module finalization. In proximity mode it waits for the saved trigger. The transformed marker position supplies command coordinates.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"authoring-rules\">Authoring rules\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Do not use aliases such as \u003ccode>CONN\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>ENTRY\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>EXIT\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>NODE\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Do not encode dimensions, directions, coordinates or rotation in sign text.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Marker replacement material is global unless the selected group entry overrides it.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>In proximity mode, every connector needs an explicit radius or a positive pack default.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "guides/pack-authoring": "\u003ch2 id=\"model\">How packs work\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A pack is a graph of reusable schematic modules. The first module comes from \u003ccode>start.group\u003c/code>; CONNECTOR markers name the group used for each next edge. A candidate is selected by weight only after the runtime confirms its configured safety checks.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"plan\">Plan the module graph\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp id=\"plan-the-module-graph\">Begin with one entrance, one repeatable path and one endpoint. Draw every connector group and its route to an endpoint. Add fallback candidates where tight terrain can reject a normal module, and add endpoint-only closing groups for connectors that may remain open at a hard limit.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"layout\">Folder layout\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>plugins/CoreStructuresX/packs/abandoned_mine/\n|-- pack.yml\n|-- structure.yml\n|-- groups.yml\n|-- commands.yml\n`-- schematics/\n    |-- entrance_01.schem\n    |-- corridor_01.schem\n    `-- endpoint_01.schem\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>commands.yml\u003c/code> is optional when no schematic has a COMMAND marker. All configured paths must stay inside this pack directory.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"schematics\">Create schematics\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Build one module with an intentional bounding box.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Place zero or one ORIGIN marker; save the clipboard origin deliberately when omitting it.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Place each CONNECTOR at the exact attachment point and face it toward the child expansion direction.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Add COMMAND markers only for trusted post-placement actions.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Save as Sponge \u003ccode>.schem\u003c/code> through the provider used by the target server.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>Test block-state rotation and block-entity NBT for chests, signs, skulls, banners, spawners and lecterns. Enable schematic entities only after testing their position, rotation and state on the exact stack.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"markers\">Marker signs\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Use only ORIGIN, CONNECTOR and COMMAND. Marker blocks are replaced during paste, while the connector, trigger and command records are persisted. See the \u003ca href=\"#/docs/instructions/marker-signs\">complete line contract\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"pack-yml\">pack.yml\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Set schema version 1, a unique safe id, display metadata, and the relative filenames for structure, groups, commands and schematics. A folder/id mismatch is allowed with a warning; duplicate declared ids disable every duplicate pack.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"structure-yml\">structure.yml\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Match the pack id. Keep \u003ccode>start.mode: MANUAL\u003c/code>, choose a start group and native facing, then configure placement offset, generation mode, limits, completion, checks and paste behavior. Keep \u003ccode>backtrack-on-blocked: false\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>require-all-connectors-resolved: true\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"groups-yml\">groups.yml\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Each dynamic group needs at least one positive-weight entry. Optional per-entry offset replaces the pack offset for that candidate. Marker replacement overrides apply only to that entry. Fallback and closing references must name existing groups; closing entries must have zero CONNECTOR markers.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"commands-yml\">commands.yml\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Each command group contains positive-weight entries. An entry may hold one string, a list, or a map of named strings. Commands run as console after the at-most-once reservation is saved. Do not place untrusted input into administrator-authored commands.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"safety\">Safety choices\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Keep one active job per instance until serial execution is proven.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Use a conservative replaceable-block whitelist.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Enable double pass only with block checking; it never bypasses pending jobs.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Start lookahead at depth 1 and increase only with measured need.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Keep module, radius, connector and global schematic limits well below accidental input sizes.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Use post-paste replacements for deliberate temporary authoring blocks.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"validate\">Validate and test\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>/csx reload\n/csx validate pack abandoned_mine\n/csx packs list\n/csx start abandoned_mine world 100 64 100 SOUTH\n/csx instance info &lt;instance-id&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Test every rotation, branch, fallback, closing route, mode, limit transition and restart. A first module that pastes correctly does not prove the complete graph.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"diagnose\">Common failures\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Missing pack: check direct folder placement, \u003ccode>pack.yml\u003c/code>, unique id and confined paths.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Invalid schematic: check markers, group ids, provider readability and configured size limits.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Blocked connector: inspect the recorded reason, fallback/closing graph, overlap, whitelist and lookahead.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Stalled automatic mode: inspect TPS, MSPT, stable samples, job delay and closing state.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Inactive proximity: check the same world, the connector state and a positive explicit/default radius.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"checklist\">Release checklist\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Zero validation errors.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>All reachable groups have a finite endpoint route.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>All rotations preserve expected block states and NBT.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Optional entities are proven on the target stack.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Largest intended expansion remains inside every hard limit and runtime budget.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Interrupted trusted jobs resume after a clean restart.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>World and plugin folders are backed up before production use.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "guides/validation-workflow": "\u003ch2 id=\"strict-yaml\">Strict YAML\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>With \u003ccode>validation.strict: true\u003c/code>, unknown keys are rejected at every fixed global, structure, group-entry, offset and command-entry level. Material maps and dynamic group ids remain intentionally dynamic.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"pack-roots\">Pack roots and ids\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The loader enumerates direct children of the packs folder without following links. Symbolic-link, junction or reparse-point pack roots are rejected. All folders are grouped by declared id before publication; every duplicate definition is disabled with diagnostics.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"confined-paths\">Confined paths\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Every pack YAML and schematic reference must be relative, lexically remain inside its configured root, and still resolve inside that root on the real filesystem. External links and sibling-prefix tricks do not pass validation.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"marker-validation\">Marker validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>At most one ORIGIN marker.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Every CONNECTOR group exists.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Every COMMAND group exists.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Every nonblank proximity radius is a positive integer.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Every connector in proximity mode has an explicit or positive default radius.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"graph-validation\">Graph validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Closing entries must be endpoints. With \u003ccode>require-all-connectors-resolvable\u003c/code>, the loader analyzes every group reachable from the start group and rejects a closed cycle or branch without a finite endpoint path.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"commands\">Validation commands\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>/csx validate\n/csx validate pack &lt;pack-id&gt;\n/csx packs list\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>The aggregate report shows its first 20 issues; use per-pack validation to inspect the complete selected report.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "guides/troubleshooting": "\u003ch2 id=\"startup\">Plugin disables on startup\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Confirm Java 21+, a compatible Paper build, and a loaded WorldEdit or FastAsyncWorldEdit provider. When the API is absent, CoreStructuresX logs the exact dependency error and disables itself safely.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"pack-not-listed\">Pack is not listed\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Confirm the folder is a normal direct child of \u003ccode>packs/\u003c/code>, contains \u003ccode>pack.yml\u003c/code>, uses a unique safe id, and does not escape through configured paths or filesystem links. Run validation and inspect the complete path in each diagnostic.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"schematic-invalid\">Schematic fails validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Check provider readability, configured axis/volume/chunk limits, ORIGIN count, connector/command group ids, positive proximity radii and referenced material names.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"does-not-expand\">Structure starts but does not expand\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Use \u003ccode>/csx instance info\u003c/code>. Inspect instance state, active jobs, open/blocked connectors, mode, generated count and quarantine count. Automatic mode may be waiting for stable TPS/MSPT samples or job delay. Proximity mode requires the player in the same world and the specific trigger active.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"overlap\">Candidate rejected for overlap\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Its transformed bounds intersect a generated module, pending job or persisted failed footprint. Move markers, shrink the schematic, add fallback/endpoint candidates, or enable a carefully bounded double pass with block checking. Pending jobs cannot be bypassed.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"blocked\">Instance is BLOCKED\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>At least one connector could not be resolved. Read the recorded reason and repair the candidate set, fallback/closing graph, overlap geometry, whitelist or lookahead constraint. CoreStructuresX does not delete prior modules to retry.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"json\">JSON cannot be loaded\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Stop Paper and back up the complete instances folder. The loader first tries the rolling \u003ccode>.json.bak\u003c/code>. If recovery cannot be completed, preserve the primary and backup, inspect the error, and repair or move the broken canonical file aside. Do not edit live state.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"quarantine\">Failed footprint remains reserved\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Inspect or repair the exact world region shown by \u003ccode>/csx instance info\u003c/code>. Only then use \u003ccode>/csx instance clear-footprint &lt;instance-id&gt; &lt;job-id&gt;\u003c/code>. The command releases the collision reservation; it does not inspect or fix blocks or entities.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "paper/config-yml": "\u003ch2 id=\"purpose\">Purpose\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>config.yml\u003c/code> owns the global pack/storage folders, marker contract, validation policy, checkpoint cadence, shared paste budgets, schematic limits, bounded caches, lookahead budget and TPS/MSPT governor.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"current-default\">Current bundled default\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/config.yml\">\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"settings\">settings and packs\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>config-version\u003c/code> must be \u003ccode>1\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>settings.debug\u003c/code> enables global diagnostic logging.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>packs.folder\u003c/code> is resolved below the plugin data folder; administrator-configured external roots are trusted only when explicitly configured and accessible.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"markers\">markers\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>header\u003c/code> defaults to \u003ccode>[CSX]\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>case-insensitive-header\u003c/code> defaults to true.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>replacements.ORIGIN\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>CONNECTOR\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>COMMAND\u003c/code> must name Bukkit block materials.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"storage\">storage\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>type\u003c/code> must be \u003ccode>JSON\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>save-connectors\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>save-triggers\u003c/code> must remain true in v1.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>checkpoint-interval-ticks\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>checkpoint-operations\u003c/code> must each be at least 1.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>force-at-phase-boundaries\u003c/code> requests a checkpoint at paste phase transitions.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"validation\">validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>strict\u003c/code> rejects unknown fixed keys with the exact YAML path.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>require-origin\u003c/code> rejects missing ORIGIN markers when true; false uses the saved clipboard origin and reports a strict-mode warning.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>require-all-connectors-resolvable\u003c/code> requires every reachable connector group to have a finite endpoint path.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"paste-budgets\">performance.paste\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Only \u003ccode>CHUNKED\u003c/code> is supported. \u003ccode>max-blocks-per-tick\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>max-milliseconds-per-tick\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>per-job-slice\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>max-active-jobs\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>max-chunk-loads-per-tick\u003c/code> are shared global budgets. Every value must be positive and the per-job slice cannot exceed the block budget.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"schematic-limits\">performance.schematics\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>max-axis\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>max-volume\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>max-chunks\u003c/code> reject oversized source/candidate geometry with overflow-safe checks. Chunk count uses the complete transformed bounding-box footprint.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"schematic-cache\">performance.schematic-cache\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Compiled sources and transformed templates have independent entry and logical-weight bounds. \u003ccode>warmup-templates: false\u003c/code> compiles variants lazily. Enabling warmup checks all referenced rotations at load time but increases startup work; the same bounds still apply.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"lookahead-budget\">performance.lookahead\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>max-simulation-nodes\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>max-milliseconds\u003c/code> bound each dry-run search. Budget exhaustion rejects that candidate instead of continuing unbounded work.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"stability\">performance.stability\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>TPS and MSPT thresholds use hysteresis. Resume TPS must be at least the pause TPS, resume MSPT must be no greater than pause MSPT, and both the sampling interval and stable-sample count must be positive.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"upgrade-note\">Upgrade note\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Existing server YAML is not merged with newly bundled defaults. Compare the installed file with this current snapshot after each update and add keys deliberately.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "paper/example-pack-yml": "\u003ch2 id=\"purpose\">Purpose\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>pack.yml\u003c/code> names one structure pack and points to its structure, group, command and schematic resources.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"bundled-example\">Bundled example\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/example-pack.yml\">\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"schema\">Schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"pack.yml schema\">\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Key\u003c/th>\u003cth>Rule\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>pack-version\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Must be 1.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>id\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Required safe id. Duplicate ids disable every duplicate definition.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>name\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Display name; defaults to id.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>version\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Pack author's version string; defaults to 1.0.0.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>author\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Defaults to unknown.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>structure\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Defaults to structure.yml.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>groups\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Defaults to groups.yml.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>commands\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Defaults to commands.yml; file is optional until a COMMAND marker references a group.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>schematics-folder\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Defaults to schematics.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"path-safety\">Path safety\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Every referenced path must be relative and remain inside the pack after normalization and real-path resolution. Absolute paths, parent traversal and external symbolic-link/junction/reparse targets are rejected.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"folder-name\">Folder name\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The folder may differ from \u003ccode>id\u003c/code>, but validation warns because matching names make administration clearer.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "paper/example-structure-yml": "\u003ch2 id=\"purpose\">Purpose\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>structure.yml\u003c/code> owns start, placement, generation mode, hard limits, completion, spatial checks and per-pack paste behavior.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"bundled-example\">Bundled example\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/example-structure.yml\">\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"identity-start\">Identity and start\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>structure-version\u003c/code> must be 1.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>id\u003c/code> must equal \u003ccode>pack.yml.id\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>enabled\u003c/code> defaults to true.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>start.mode\u003c/code> must be \u003ccode>MANUAL\u003c/code>; \u003ccode>start.group\u003c/code> must exist.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"placement\">Placement\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>native-facing\u003c/code> accepts NORTH, EAST, SOUTH or WEST. \u003ccode>offset.forward\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>left\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>right\u003c/code> are non-negative; \u003ccode>up\u003c/code> may be signed. Legacy \u003ccode>height\u003c/code> remains an alias for \u003ccode>up\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"generation\">Generation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>mode\u003c/code>: \u003ccode>AUTOMATIC\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>PLAYER_PROXIMITY\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Automatic order supports \u003ccode>NEAREST_TO_ORIGIN\u003c/code> then \u003ccode>FIFO\u003c/code>; \u003ccode>job-delay\u003c/code> is non-negative ticks.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Lookahead depth is 0–10 and at least 1 when enabled; policy is \u003ccode>ALL_CONNECTORS\u003c/code> or \u003ccode>ANY_CONNECTOR\u003c/code>.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>backtrack-on-blocked\u003c/code> must remain false.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Proximity check interval accepts ticks such as \u003ccode>20t\u003c/code>; default radius is non-negative.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"limits-completion\">Limits and completion\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>max-modules\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>max-radius\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>max-open-connectors\u003c/code> must be at least 1. \u003ccode>require-all-connectors-resolved\u003c/code> must remain true. \u003ccode>enter-closing-when-limits-reached\u003c/code> controls whether remaining connectors try closing groups.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"space-check\">Space checks\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Overlap mode is \u003ccode>SCHEMATIC_BOUNDING_BOX\u003c/code>; padding is non-negative. Double pass requires enabled \u003ccode>WHITELIST\u003c/code> block checking. Replaceable materials and post-paste replacements must be valid Bukkit blocks.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"paste\">Per-pack paste\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Mode must be \u003ccode>CHUNKED\u003c/code>. The pack block budget and per-instance active-job limit must be positive. \u003ccode>paste-air\u003c/code> controls source air; \u003ccode>paste-entities\u003c/code> opts into schematic entity placement.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "paper/example-groups-yml": "\u003ch2 id=\"purpose\">Purpose\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>groups.yml\u003c/code> maps connector group ids to weighted schematic candidates and optional fallback/closing routes.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"bundled-example\">Bundled example\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/example-groups.yml\">\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"group-schema\">Group schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>groups-version: 1\ngroups:\n  path:\n    entries:\n      - schematic: corridor_01.schem\n        weight: 10\n    fallback-groups:\n      - rooms\n    closing-groups:\n      - endpoints\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Every group id is dynamic but must be safe. Every group needs at least one valid entry, and every fallback/closing reference must exist.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"entry-schema\">Entry schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Each entry requires a confined schematic path and positive integer weight. It may provide an \u003ccode>offset\u003c/code>, marker \u003ccode>replacements\u003c/code>, and \u003ccode>allow-overlap-with-parent\u003c/code>. Legacy aliases \u003ccode>height\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>overlap-on-parent\u003c/code> remain accepted.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"offsets-replacements\">Offsets and replacements\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>An entry offset replaces the pack placement offset for that selected schematic. Replacement keys are ORIGIN, CONNECTOR and COMMAND; omitted keys keep global materials. Overrides affect paste planning, not marker detection.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"fallbacks\">Fallback groups\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>After all normal candidates fail, fallback groups are tried in listed order. Failed incremental recipes are remembered so one connector does not immediately repeat the same rejected work.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"closing-groups\">Closing groups\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Every closing entry must reference an endpoint schematic with zero CONNECTOR markers. Completion occurs only after no open connector and no active job remains.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "paper/example-commands-yml": "\u003ch2 id=\"purpose\">Purpose\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>commands.yml\u003c/code> defines weighted command groups referenced by COMMAND marker line 3. The bundled test pack intentionally has no command groups.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"bundled-example\">Bundled example\u003c/h2>\n\u003cdiv class=\"config-file-mount\" data-config-file=\"paper/example-commands.yml\">\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"schema\">Schema\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>commands-version: 1\ngroups:\n  finish_room:\n    entries:\n      - weight: 1\n        commands:\n          - \"say module {module} finished at {world} {x} {y} {z}\"\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Each group needs at least one valid positive-weight entry. \u003ccode>commands\u003c/code> may be one string, a list, or a map whose values are non-empty strings. One leading slash is optional and removed before dispatch.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"placeholders\">Placeholders\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>{world} {x} {x+N} {y} {y+N} {z} {z+N}\n{instance} {module} {schematic} {group} {source_group}\n{uuid} {origin_x} {origin_y} {origin_z}\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Coordinates are the transformed COMMAND marker position. Signed short offsets such as \u003ccode>{y-2}\u003c/code> are supported; out-of-range forms are left unchanged. The marker UUID is persisted across restarts.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"delivery-semantics\">Delivery semantics\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Structural completion is committed first. Then the command record is marked consumed and saved before console dispatch. A crash after reservation but before Paper accepts the command can skip it; CoreStructuresX deliberately does not replay an external side effect.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>A false dispatch result or exception is logged and not counted as successful, but the reservation remains consumed.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "runtime/instance-persistence": "\u003ch2 id=\"data-version\">Data version 5\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Every current canonical instance uses data version 5. The filename is derived from a safe \u003ccode>[a-z0-9_-]+\u003c/code> instance id. Filename/id mismatches, unsafe ids and duplicate definitions are excluded before publication.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"saved-state\">Saved state\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The JSON graph includes origin, mode overrides, generated modules, spatial bounds, connectors, proximity triggers, command reservations, lifecycle state, sequences and complete recoverable paste journals.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"revisions\">Revisions and ordered checkpoints\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The server thread assigns monotonic revisions and captures detached state only when a checkpoint is due. One ordered daemon writer serializes, flushes and atomically replaces snapshots. Per-instance submissions are coalesced and stale revisions cannot replace newer state.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"checkpoint-schedule\">Checkpoint schedule\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The global interval, operation threshold and phase-boundary flag determine periodic cursor checkpoints. Transactional lifecycle changes, first-mutation intent, finalization and shutdown still use synchronous commits where durability gates a world/runtime effect.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"finalization\">Finalization\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A paste enters \u003ccode>FINALIZING\u003c/code> with its job record still recoverable. The complete detached final state is saved before new module, connector, trigger or command state becomes visible. A failed final commit leaves finalization pending for retry.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"restart-validation\">Restart validation\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Startup rebuilds jobs only when pack, schematic, transformed paste recipe, operation counts and invariants match the journal. A mismatch blocks the job and parent connector instead of continuing with changed inputs.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"checkpoint-failure\">Checkpoint failure\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A failed asynchronous checkpoint pauses the affected instance, releases its chunk tickets, records the reason and prevents further mutation until the storage problem is corrected and the instance is resumed.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "runtime/backup-and-recovery": "\u003ch2 id=\"before-repair\">Before manual repair\u003c/h2>\n\u003col>\n\u003cli>Stop Paper.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Back up the affected worlds.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Back up the complete \u003ccode>plugins/CoreStructuresX/data/instances/\u003c/code> directory.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Preserve the primary, rolling backup and every migration/invalid/corrupt evidence file.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ol>\n\u003ch2 id=\"atomic-saves\">Atomic saves and rolling backup\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A save writes and fsyncs \u003ccode>&lt;instance&gt;.json.tmp\u003c/code>, retains the previous valid primary as \u003ccode>&lt;instance&gt;.json.bak\u003c/code>, and atomically replaces the canonical file when supported. Filesystems without atomic move support use a same-directory replacement fallback.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"corrupt-primary\">Corrupt primary\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>If the primary cannot be parsed, the loader tries the rolling backup. A valid backup is accepted only when its instance id matches. The bad primary is preserved as \u003ccode>.json.corrupt\u003c/code> with a numeric suffix when needed, then the backup is restored through a flushed temporary file.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"migration\">Version migration\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Unversioned data is treated as v1. Versions 1 through 4 are copied to \u003ccode>.json.vN.bak\u003c/code> before migration to v5. V1/v2 active jobs lack a trusted checksum journal and become failed with blocked processing connectors. V3 journals keep trusted checksum recovery state. V4 failed/active footprints are reconstructed conservatively.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"invalid-files\">Invalid and duplicate files\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Unsafe ids, filename/id mismatches and duplicate instance ids are not loaded. Their canonical candidates are moved without overwrite to unique \u003ccode>.json.invalid[.N]\u003c/code> files so evidence is not lost.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"failed-footprint\">Failed-footprint quarantine\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A failed job that may have mutated its bounded region keeps that region reserved in the world spatial index, including after restart. Inspect or repair the region first. Then run:\u003c/p>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>/csx instance clear-footprint &lt;instance-id&gt; &lt;job-id&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>The command synchronously saves the removal of the reservation. It does not inspect, restore or delete any block, block entity or schematic entity.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"no-backtracking\">No destructive backtracking\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Do not set \u003ccode>backtrack-on-blocked\u003c/code> true. Prior terrain, fluids, block-entity NBT, spawned entities, dispatched commands and later player/plugin changes cannot be reconstructed losslessly.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "reference/command-reference": "\u003cdiv class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"CoreStructuresX command reference\">\u003ctable>\n\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Command\u003c/th>\u003cth>Permission\u003c/th>\u003cth>Behavior\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\n\u003ctbody>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>None for help\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Shows the administrative command list.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx reload\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.reload\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Reloads config and packs only when no paste job is queued, running, paused or finalizing.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx validate [pack &lt;pack-id&gt;]\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.validate\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Shows aggregate or complete selected-pack validation diagnostics.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx packs list\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.packs\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Lists pack identity, validation state and schematic count.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx start &lt;pack-id&gt; [group-id] [world x y z facing] [automatic|proximity &lt;radius&gt;] [debug|verbose] [actionbar]\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.start\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Starts one instance with optional group, location, mode and monitoring overrides.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx instances list\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.instances\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Lists state, pack, progress, elapsed time, modules and open connectors.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx instance info &lt;instance-id&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.instances\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Shows lifecycle, mode, progress, jobs, quarantines, triggers, modules and blocked connectors.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx instance pause &lt;instance-id&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.instances\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Persists PAUSED state, preserves cursors and releases owned chunk tickets.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx instance resume &lt;instance-id&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.instances\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Resumes only a valid PAUSED graph.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx instance stop &lt;instance-id&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.instances\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Moves an idle instance to terminal STOPPED without deleting world content.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003ctr>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>/csx instance clear-footprint &lt;instance-id&gt; &lt;job-id&gt;\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.instances\u003c/code>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>After operator inspection, releases one persisted FAILED-job collision reservation.\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n\u003ch2 id=\"start-sender\">Start sender rules\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>A player may omit location; the command uses the player's block position and snaps yaw to a cardinal facing. Console must supply world, integer x/y/z and NORTH, EAST, SOUTH or WEST. \u003ccode>actionbar\u003c/code> requires a player sender.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"mode-overrides\">Mode overrides\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>\u003ccode>automatic\u003c/code>/\u003ccode>auto\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>proximity\u003c/code>/\u003ccode>player_proximity\u003c/code>/\u003ccode>player-proximity &lt;radius&gt;\u003c/code> are accepted. The optional word \u003ccode>type\u003c/code> is accepted before the mode. Overrides are stored on the instance and do not edit \u003ccode>structure.yml\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"lifecycle-safety\">Lifecycle safety\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Pause does not make reload safe. Stop is rejected while an active or finalizing job exists. Clear-footprint applies only to a failed quarantined job and never repairs the world.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "reference/permission-reference": "\u003ch2 id=\"umbrella\">Umbrella permission\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>This node grants every administrative child and defaults to operators.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"children\">Individual permissions\u003c/h2>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>corestructuresx.admin.reload\ncorestructuresx.admin.validate\ncorestructuresx.admin.packs\ncorestructuresx.admin.start\ncorestructuresx.admin.instances\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003cp>Every child also defaults to operators. Each command handler accepts either its specific child or the umbrella permission.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"recommended-split\">Recommended split\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Builders may receive validation and pack listing without start or instance mutation. Restrict start, pause/resume/stop and clear-footprint to trusted administrators because they can paste content or change live recovery reservations.\u003c/p>\n\u003cpre tabindex=\"0\">\u003ccode>lp group builder permission set corestructuresx.admin.validate true\nlp group builder permission set corestructuresx.admin.packs true\nlp group admin permission set corestructuresx.admin true\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\n\u003ch2 id=\"command-markers\">Command marker trust\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Permission nodes control the CoreStructuresX admin command. They do not sandbox console commands authored inside a pack. Limit filesystem and pack-authoring access separately.\u003c/p>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "reference/production-checklist": "\u003ch2 id=\"runtime\">Runtime\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Paper starts cleanly with Java 21+ and a loaded WorldEdit or FAWE provider.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>The exact Paper/provider combination has been tested with this plugin version.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Worlds, plugin data and pack sources have a tested backup and restore path.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"pack\">Pack\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ccode>/csx validate\u003c/code> reports zero errors.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Every referenced schematic exists inside the configured folder.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Every reachable connector group has a finite endpoint route.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Fallback and endpoint-only closing groups have been exercised.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Every rotation preserves intended block states, signs, inventories, spawners, skulls, banners and lecterns.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Optional entities are tested on the target Paper/provider build before \u003ccode>paste-entities\u003c/code> is enabled.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"limits\">Limits and performance\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Module, radius and open-connector caps fit the intended largest structure.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Global axis, volume and chunk-footprint limits accept production schematics without allowing accidental huge inputs.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Block/time/job/chunk-load budgets have been measured with loaded and unloaded chunks.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>TPS/MSPT pause and resume behavior is observed under load.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>High-branching lookahead stops inside its configured node/time bounds.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"recovery\">Persistence and recovery\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Automatic and proximity instances survive a normal restart.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Interrupted trusted phased jobs resume from persisted cursors.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Connectors, triggers and command UUIDs remain present after restart.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Rolling backup recovery and the manual stop/back-up/repair procedure are understood.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Clear-footprint is restricted to operators who can inspect the exact failed region.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003ch2 id=\"access\">Access\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>Start and instance-management permissions are limited to trusted administrators.\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>Pack authors understand that COMMAND markers execute as console.\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003chr>\n",
  "reference/documentation-scope": "\u003ch2 id=\"source-baseline\">Source baseline\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>This documentation describes CoreStructuresX 2026.1.1 from the current plugin manifest, bundled YAML resources and project-owned Java source at commit \u003ccode>1fced01406b6c7afb51f6b2f9659ad7993f39ba2\u003c/code>.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"configuration-snapshots\">Configuration snapshots\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>The five displayed YAML files are allowlisted snapshots: global \u003ccode>config.yml\u003c/code> plus the bundled test pack's \u003ccode>pack.yml\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>structure.yml\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>groups.yml\u003c/code> and \u003ccode>commands.yml\u003c/code>. Binary schematics and plugin artifacts are excluded.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The website workflow may refresh those files from the private plugin repository using read-only credentials. No token belongs in browser JavaScript, HTML, generated bundles, logs or public URLs.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"compatibility\">Compatibility claims\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Java 21, Paper 1.21.11 and WorldEdit 7.4.3 are build/documentation boundaries. FAWE is accepted as a runtime provider without a pinned project dependency. Source inspection does not prove every runtime combination; test the exact versions used by the server.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"runtime-evidence\">Runtime evidence\u003c/h2>\n\u003cp>Statements about persistence, recovery and generation describe implemented source contracts. This website does not claim a live server test unless a release note or separately identified test report says so.\u003c/p>\n\u003ch2 id=\"public-links\">Public links\u003c/h2>\n\u003cul>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://modrinth.com/plugin/corestructuresx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CoreStructuresX on Modrinth\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/IceWolf23X/CoreStructuresX-issues/issues\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Issue tracker\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"https://bstats.org/plugin/bukkit/CoreStructuresX\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Anonymous bStats dashboard\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\n\u003c/ul>\n\u003chr>\n"
};
  var docs = window.COREX_DOCS;
  if (!docs || !Array.isArray(docs.articles)) throw new Error('Load docs-content.js before docs-bodies.js.');
  // Restore the bodyHtml contract consumed by the wiki, search and full reference.
  docs.articles.forEach(function (article) {
    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(bodies, article.id)) throw new Error('Documentation bundle missing article: ' + article.id);
    article.bodyHtml = bodies[article.id];
  });
}());
